# Backend Python

## Layering

- `app/routes/api.py` — thin handlers, `jsonify()`, no vendor HTTP
- `app/services/` — business logic
- `app/clients/` — HTTP clients (SEC, Stooq); no Flask imports
- `app/repositories.py` — SQL only; upserts with `ON CONFLICT`
- `app/workers/` — job handlers; drain `ingestion_jobs`

## Required patterns

```python
# SEC: Host header must match URL host (www.sec.gov vs data.sec.gov)
response = session.get(url, headers=client.headers_for(url))

# Admin errors: JSON body, not bare 500
return jsonify({"error": str(exc)}), 500
```

## Data rules

- Multiple tickers can share one CIK — `companies.cik` is not unique.
- Request-time routes read SQLite first; Nasdaq only as optional fallback.
- Long ETL (feeds, SEC bulk) belongs in worker jobs or bootstrap, not blocking reads.

## Tests

- Fixtures: `app`, `client` from `app/tests/conftest.py`
- Mock HTTP; no live SEC/Stooq in unit tests
- Run: `python -m pytest app/tests/ -q`
